  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This guide is for the version of the Air Genasi published in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Monsters of the Multiverse",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/motm/fantastical-races#AirGenasiTraits"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". For the classic version of the Genasi, see our "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Genasi Handbook",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/races/genasi/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Air Genasi is a descendent of Djinni, genies from the elemental plane of\n\tair. This is reflected in their traits by above-average speed, the ability to\n\thold their breath indefinitely, lightning resistance, and innate spellcasting\n\twith a clear thematic link to the plane of air."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While the Air Genasi’s traits aren’t overwhelmingly strong, their innate spellcasting is a good basis for almost any spellcaster. Shocking Grasp isn’t a great spell, but it might save you a cantrip at low levels where full casters only get two or three cantrips. Feather Fall is a staple in any party, and Levitate is a weirdly effective combination of utility and save-or-suck. Classes that aren’t full casters will likely find the Air Genasi underwhelming, but classes like the Cleric may find the Air Genasi’s spells appealing since clerics don’t get any of those spells. They also get Darkvision, which is always welcome."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
